proton-autogen (3.4.5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Thanks to all users and contributors for their continued support, feedback and bug reports.
  * Interface:
  *
  * Introduced a new Cute visual style.
  * Improved CSS styling and interface consistency.
  * Replaced checkbox controls with switch buttons.
  * Added text background styling.
  * Game Editor:
  *
  * Added variable autocompletion with an integrated search menu.
  * Improved variable selection and editing workflow.
  * Environment variables:
  *
  * Added WINE_FULLSCREEN_FSR_STRENGTH.
  * Added new environment variables for GE-Proton 11-12.
  * Improved environment variable descriptions and documentation.
  * Internationalization:
  *
  * Added Hungarian (hu) language support.
  * Expanded translations for Japanese, Kurdish, Dutch, Polish, Hungarian, Vietnamese, Thai and Bulgarian.
  * Updated multilingual documentation.
  *
  * Added new backend configuration options to provide greater control over application behavior.
  * Added an option to disable .EXE file scanning for improved scan customization.
  * Improved scan configuration and finalized additional scanning options.
  * Optimized scan filtering and filtering operations to improve scanning efficiency.
  * Improved overall scanning performance and internal processing.
  * Refactored library.normalize_games to improve game data normalization and code maintainability.
  * Refactored UX components and improved separation between application logic and presentation.
  * Moved color_label and desc into the UX layer to improve architecture and component organization.
  * Improved headless module imports to support cleaner operation without graphical interface dependencies.
  * Cleaned up imports and internal code organization.
  * Improved CSS mode optimization and styling performance.
  * Fixed various CSS and UI styling issues.
  * Improved --profile option handling and added associated tests.
  * Improved application version handling and corrected version-related issues.
  * Added and improved automated tests for UX components and refactored modules.
  * Improved code quality through refactoring, cleanup and additional regression testing.
  * Strengthened multi-distribution Linux build and compatibility validation.
  * Improved Debian package build and release validation.
  * Improved AUR package validation and automated checks.
  * Strengthened package build workflows and release reliability.
  * General backend, UX, performance, configuration handling and code maintainability improvements.

